source.text:
\begin{proof}
By the definition of a Dedekind algebra, $N = \closureofunder{s}{o}$.
Now if both ${o} \in X$ and $(\forall {n} \in N)(n \in X \lif
{s}({n}) \in X)$, then $N = \closureofunder{s}{o} \subseteq X$.
\end{proof}

