\begin{cor}\ollabel{natinductionschema}
Let $N, s, o$ comprise a Dedekind algebra. Then for any formula
$\phi(x)$, which may have parameters:
\begin{center}
	if $\phi(o)$ and $(\forall {n} \in N)(\phi(n)\lif
	\phi({s}({n})))$, {then} $(\forall n \in N)\phi(n)$
\end{center}
\end{cor}

